ame=07ae2d32-1050-4e80-96ff-eb2d98378d4e.pdf"},{"period":"Jan 2026","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=d70edbab-d5b2-47ae-8820-efacc5052d13.pdf"},{"period":"Dec 2025","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=d59af2b6-34c7-4ca1-9455-f4899e5f26cf.pdf"},{"period":"Nov 2025","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=7fa78f01-221c-47fe-a83d-098bc43b0de7.pdf"},{"period":"Oct 2025","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=56f7fbb9-5cf4-49e1-95ef-62af7ad2a999.pdf"}]},"as_of":"2026-11-15T18:52:40+05:30","research":{"summary":"TCS is India's largest IT services company, reporting Q2 FY27 (Sept 2026) revenue of ₹73,188 crore with 0.5% QoQ constant-currency growth and 24% operating margin. Growth is broadening across international markets and AI revenue crossed $3.1 billion annualized (over 10% of revenue), though margins face investment and MHP-related headwinds.","how_it_makes_money":"Revenue comes from IT services across verticals — BFSI (largest, +2.5% QoQ), Manufacturing, Technology & Services, Consumer Business, Life Sciences, and ERU — plus regional markets including India; AI services now exceed 10% of overall revenue.","bull":[{"point":"AI revenue scaling fast and at higher margins than company average","quote":"the $3.1 billion AI revenues which we have are coming in at a much higher margin than our company average","page":22,"url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=7dc14216-f892-46f1-bf82-5c7b387a83b9.pdf","source":"Earnings call, Oct 2026"},{"point":"Broad-based international growth with strong BFSI","quote":"BFSI was our strongest large vertical and the largest contributor to growth, with 2.5% sequential and 3.9% year-on-year growth in constant currency","page":10,"url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=7dc14216-f892-46f1-bf82-5c7b387a83b9.pdf","source":"Earnings call, Oct 2026"},{"point":"Healthy order book excluding large pending deals","quote":"TCV for the quarter was US$9.6 billion. This excludes the Porsche and Best Buy deals","page":3,"url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=7dc14216-f892-46f1-bf82-5c7b387a83b9.pdf","source":"Earnings call, Oct 2026"}],"bear":[{"point":"Margin path to 25-26% uncertain amid rising subcontracting and investment costs","quote":"While it's an uphill task, we'll continue to endeavor to inch up on our margins","page":16,"url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=7dc14216-f892-46f1-bf82-5c7b387a83b9.pdf","source":"Earnings call, Oct 2026"},{"point":"MHP acquisition dilutes margins ~50bps in H2","quote":"The acquisition-related dilution, particularly in MHP, is likely to impact by about 50 basis points depending on the timing of closure","page":16,"url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=7dc14216-f892-46f1-bf82-5c7b387a83b9.pdf","source":"Earnings call, Oct 2026"},{"point":"AI deflation risk not yet over; Consumer and ERU declined","quote":"I don't want to conclude by saying that the deﬂation part is complete","page":13,"url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=7dc14216-f892-46f1-bf82-5c7b387a83b9.pdf","source":"Earnings call, Oct 2026"}],"watch":[{"point":"Whether India project deferral revenue returns and regional markets stabilize","quote":"In India, we had a project deferral, which caused this revenue decrease","page":13,"url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=7dc14216-f892-46f1-bf82-5c7b387a83b9.pdf","source":"Earnings call, Oct 2026"},{"point":"Whether margins can inch toward 25% exit FY27 despite headwinds","quote":"we'd look towards inching up from where we are, whilst not losing sight of prioritizing investments for growth","page":20,"url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=7dc14216-f892-46f1-bf82-5c7b387a83b9.pdf","source":"Earnings call, Oct 2026"}],"sources":["Earnings call, Oct 2026"],"as_of":"2026-11-15T18:52:44+05:30"}}